::kind(writ)

=[ Writ: unparseable fixture ]

A writ that cannot be parsed at all. The closing `}` is missing.

This is what dropping a line out of a rule now looks like: the parameters
live inside the entry, so losing one takes the group's closer with it and
the file stops parsing. It used to be possible for a declaration to come
detached and simply vanish -- see `layers-bare`.

==[ crate-layering ]

@rule(crate-layering){
  guard: { twrit: layers }

  layers: {
    0: list("thing")
